A :FOR header split after a trailing `:TO` or `:STEP`: no `;` is forced
after the keyword (fmt.semicolon_enforcement "the line ends with :TO /
:STEP"), and the operand line takes one continuation level, the same
column as the loop body. The form with `:TO` / `:STEP` leading the next
line is left out: range-formatting those lines re-indents them, an A2
invariant failure reported separately.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE SplitFor;
:PARAMETERS nLimit;
:DECLARE i, nSum, nDown;
nSum := 0;
nDown := -1;
:FOR i := 1 :TO
nLimit;
nSum += i;
:NEXT;
:FOR i := nLimit :TO 1 :STEP
nDown;
nSum -= i;
:NEXT;
:RETURN nSum;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE SplitFor;
	:PARAMETERS nLimit;
	:DECLARE i, nSum, nDown;
	nSum := 0;
	nDown := -1;
	:FOR i := 1 :TO
		nLimit;
		nSum += i;
	:NEXT;

	:FOR i := nLimit :TO 1 :STEP
		nDown;
		nSum -= i;
	:NEXT;
	:RETURN nSum;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
